# =====================================================================================
# gate_identity_neg.ttl — the FAILING NEGATIVE fixture for GateIdentityShape (W2 · SP0, T-GATES).
# The materialized RED (D24: sh:conforms true alone is vacuous — a positive AND a failing negative
# per shape).
# =====================================================================================
# A SECOND gate:specification record whose gate:identifier COLLIDES with the committed V0 syntax
# gate (gates/gates.ttl gdata:gate:identifier "algebra:gate:V0:syntax" — the SINGLE injected
# violation). Merged onto the algebra data graph the graph MUST NOT conform: GateIdentityShape's
# sh:select (shapes/algebra.shapes.ttl) returns both this node and the real V0 gate sharing one
# gate:identifier, so it flips conforms True->False. It is the reference gate-identity uniqueness
# tooth biting (consolidated.shacl.ttl:1317-1327 'gateIdentifier must identify at most one
# GateSpecification'). It carries only its type + colliding identifier, so no other shape fires.
#
# Depth-gate compliance: the subject is an owl:NamedIndividual with a SPECIFIC type
# (core:entity:structure:class:gate:specification), never an owl:Class — so no ≥200-char
# rdfs:comment is required on a fixture node.

@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix cls:   <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:core:entity:structure:class:> .
@prefix gdata: <urn:silmaril:type:graph:instance:instruction:code:property:core:entity:property:data:> .

<urn:silmaril:fixture:algebra:gate:identity:negative>
    a owl:NamedIndividual , cls:gate:specification ;
    gdata:gate:identifier "algebra:gate:V0:syntax" .
    # INJECTED VIOLATION: reuses the committed V0 gate:identifier -> GateIdentityShape RED
